Author: Lisardowo <lisardowo@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Nov 15 12:28:25 2026 -0600

    Integrate API.Server into main.go, keep robustness, add tests

    - main.go uses API.Server: /api/catalog, /api/regions, /api/status,
      /api/filters, GET+POST /api/analog and /api/custom/* are now served.
    - --own-regions is parsed, enables /api/custom/* and is logged at startup.
    - POST /api/analog takes the AnalogRequest body (Calculate -> Analog rename
      from main); /api/calculate removed. Status unchanged; data/status.png
      taken from main.
    - Robustness is part of the API response; Model.AnalyzeRobustness works with
      custom variables and missions.
    - CORS: GET/POST/DELETE, any localhost origin when ALLOWED_ORIGIN is empty.
    - Router 404/405 replies are JSON.
    - Tests for API, custom and jsonParser; example upload files; API/README.md.
    - Add missing trailing newlines (gofmt).

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
